                "description": "a scalar colouring the deformed solid: on the reference grid, its cell grid, or the nodes or cells of the displacement's mesh (e.g. an element stress); default: the view field when it lives there"
              },
              "grid_every": {
                "type": "integer",
                "minimum": 0,
                "maximum": 64,
                "description": "draw every n-th deformed reference grid line (0: none)"
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": [
              "field"
            ],
            "description": "draw a deformed solid on top: reference cells (grid cells, their Freudenthal-Kuhn simplices, or mesh triangles/tetrahedra) moved by scale x displacement; planar frames show the solid's section with its outline, iso (3-D) frames its deformed boundary surface (clipped with its cut as the cap) over a section plane of the view field"
          },
          "iso": {
